      }

OUTCOME PROJECTION: NO-OP PORT.
  - Page accesses are already snake_case and match wire shape exactly (signal, type, severity,
    value, baseline, z_score, detected_at, message, health_summary, signals_monitored,
    anomalies_last_7d, anomalies_last_24h).
  - No useSettings / convertX / SI-named field references in the entire features/diagnostics tree
    (verified via grep for: useSettings|convertDistance|convertTemp|convertSpeed|convertPressure|
     convertEnergy|miles_to|temp_c|temp_f|speed_mph|battery_temp|inside_temp|outside_temp|
     charge_rate|distance_mi|range_km|range_mi|odometer -> 0 matches).
  - Anomaly detection is signal-agnostic: value/baseline/z_score are unitless statistical
    quantities computed from raw signal_log values. Applying convertXFromSI to a z-score or
    a generic-signal raw value would distort/destroy the data — same correctness rationale as
    Phase-43/0024 for telemetry generic raw-signal viewers and /0036 for onboarding boolean
    flags. The display intentionally renders 'value' / 'baseline' as raw fmtNumber(_, 2) and
    'z_score' as fmtNumber(_, 1) followed by sigma glyph.
  - Hook URL '/analytics/anomalies?vehicle_id=...&days=...' has NO /api/v1/ prefix and uses
    snake_case query params -- conformant per audit rule #7+#8.
  - Page imports already use shared component barrels: @/components/layout, @/components/ui,
    @/components/data-display, @/components/charts (no direct recharts), @/components/feedback,
    @/components/motion -- conformant per audit rules #2+#3+#10.
  - No raw <button>/<input>/<textarea>/<select>/<table> elements -- uses Select from
    @/components/ui (line 10) -- conformant per audit rule #2.
  - No inline style attribute with var(--*) -- uses className with text-[var(--text-primary)]
    arbitrary-value Tailwind syntax which is className not inline style -- conformant per audit
    rule #1.

