=== NOTES ===
1. NO-OP-PORT outcome (no source code changes): features/diagnostics contains a single
   production page (AnomalyDashboardPage.tsx) that renders generic anomaly-detection
   metadata -- z-scores, baselines, signal-frequency counts, severity enums, health-status
   strings -- none of which are physical-unit quantities. SI conversion would be
   semantically incorrect because the same .value field carries different units depending
   on the .signal name (BatteryLevel%, TpmsPressure Pa, RatedRange m, ...) and anomaly
   detection treats them as unitless statistical observations. Same outcome pattern as
   Phase-43/0024 (telemetry generic raw-signal viewers), /0031 (automations logical
   configurators), /0032 (notifications alert metadata), /0033 (admin infrastructure
   surfaces), /0034 (settings preferences UI), /0036 (onboarding boolean flags).

2. Hook fully conformant pre-port: useAnomalies.ts uses request<AnomalyData>('/analytics/
   anomalies?vehicle_id=...&days=...') with no /api/v1/ prefix and snake_case query params;
   AnomalyData + AnomalyEntry interface fields match backend wire shape exactly per byte-
   for-byte JSON-tag verification at internal/api/anomaly_handler.go:27-43. No @deprecated
   tag needed because the route is alive at internal/api/router.go:1117. No type drift
   between hook interface and api/types.ts because AnomalyData is not declared in
   api/types.ts -- locked-policy precedent from Phase-43/0036 OnboardingStatus and /0034
   PollingConfig kept inline because no other consumer needs the type.

3. Page count baseline=1 (sole production page) preserved at after=1.

4. PowerShell-7 quirks reused from prior Phase-43 prompts (no new ones encountered):
   (a) Resolve-Path absolute on .github\prompts\db-refactor\logs\phase-43-0038-domain-diagnostics.log BEFORE Push-Location web -- else Tee-Object loses the
       file under web\.github\* during the BUILD section (Phase-46/64 + Phase-43/0021..0037).
   (b) .\node_modules\.bin\tsc.cmd and npm.cmd run build instead of npx tsc / npm run build
       to dodge npm 10's executable-resolution quirk (Phase-43/0021..0037).
   (c) Audit regex literals expressed as single-quoted PowerShell strings with [''"]
       character class (single-quote-escaped via doubling) -- the prompt's verbatim
       ['\""] doubled-double-quote-escape parses correctly here under inline pwsh because
       the powershell tool feeds the command through pwsh -Command rather than -File, but
       the single-quoted form is more robust across both invocation styles.
   (d) git status --porcelain parsed by Substring(3).Trim() and -like "*" matching
       instead of [regex]::Escape on Windows backslash paths -- porcelain output uses
       forward slashes regardless of OS, and -like is more predictable than -match
       (Phase-43/0033..0037 NOTES).
   (e) .github/prompts/ is gitignored per .gitignore:83-89 + repo memory so git status
       --porcelain returns empty for the log file even after Add-Content writes -- the
       allowed-files / disallowed-files check correctly sees zero entries because the log
       is invisible to git until git add -f stages it; commit step uses git add -f to
       force-track the log artifact (Phase-43/0036 same pattern).

5. Page-content audit walk-down (verifying baseline conformance even though file unchanged):
   - imports from @/components/{layout,ui,data-display,charts,feedback,motion} barrels --
     no direct recharts/leaflet/framer-motion;
   - no raw <button|input|textarea|select|table> elements -- uses Select from @/components/ui;
